\v 3 \add That day,\add* four¦175430 men¦175431 \add who were isolated due to\add* a¦175433 skin¦175433 disease¦175433 \add ≈were at the city\add* gate¦175435, and¦175436 they¦175436 \add ≈asked¦175436 each¦175437 other\add*, “Why¦175441 are¦175442 we¦175442 \add just\add* sitting¦175443 here¦175444 until¦175445 we¦175447 \add ≈starve\add*?
\v 4 If¦175449 we \add ≈go into the city, we'll¦175456 starve to death¦175456 in there¦175457, but¦175458\add* if¦175458 we¦175460 sit¦175460 here¦175461, we'll¦175462 die¦175462 \add anyway\add*. \add ^Why don't\add* \add ≈we go into¦175466 the¦175468 Aramean army camp¦175468\add*—if¦175470 they¦175472 kill us¦175472 then we'll¦175473 die, but¦175474 if¦175474 they¦175476 let us¦175476 live, then¦175477 we'll¦175477 live.”
