\v 8 \add ≈So¦175556\add* those¦175557 \add four\add* \add ≈men with leprosy¦175557 approached\add* the¦175561 edge¦175561 of¦175561 the¦175562 camp¦175562 and¦175563 went¦175563 \add ≈into¦175564 the first\add* tent¦175566, and¦175568 ate¦175568 and¦175569 drank¦175569. Then¦175570 they¦175570 \add ≈took¦175570 some\add* gold¦175573 and silver¦175572 and¦175574 clothes¦175574 out, and¦175575 they¦175575 went¦175575 and¦175576 hid¦175576 it. Then¦175577 they¦175577 returned¦175577 and¦175578 went¦175578 into¦175579 another¦175582 tent, and¦175583 \add ≈stole some stuff\add* from¦175584 that one¦175567, and¦175585 went¦175585 and¦175586 hid¦175586 that.
\v 9 Then¦175588 they¦175588 said¦175588 \add ≈to each¦175589 other\add*, “\add ≈We¦175597 shouldn't¦175593 really be¦175598 doing¦175598 this¦175600 today\add*. It's a¦175601 day¦175601 of¦175601 good news¦175603, but¦175605 we've¦175605 been¦175606 \add ≈keeping it to ourselves\add*. \add If\add* we¦175607 wait¦175607 until¦175608 the¦175610 light¦175610 of¦175610 the¦175611 morning¦175611, \add ≈we'll get punished¦175613 for it¦175612\add*, \add ≈so\add* let's¦175616 go¦175616 now¦175614 and¦175617 inform the¦175619 king's¦175619 household¦175618.”
\v 10 \add ≈So¦175621\add* they¦175621 went¦175621 and¦175622 called¦175622 out¦175622 to¦175623 one of¦175625 the¦175626 city¦175626 \add #gatekeepers¦175625\add*, and¦175627 they¦175627 informed¦175627 them¦175628, “We¦175630 went¦175630 to¦175631 the¦175633 Aramean camp¦175633, but¦175635 listen¦175635, there¦175636 \add ≈wasn't¦175636 anyone there, or any voices¦175640\add*. The¦175645 horses¦175645 and¦175647 donkeys¦175647 were¦175648 still tethered¦175648, and¦175649 the¦175649 tents¦175649 were left just¦175650 as¦175650 they¦175652 were¦175652.”
