\p
\v 17 The¦175795 king¦175795 had appointed¦175796 the¦175799 captain¦175799 who¦175800 \add ≈had argued with Elisha to be¦175802 in charge at\add* the¦175808 \add city\add* gate¦175808, but¦175809 the¦175810 people¦175810 trampled¦175809 him¦175809 \add *there\add* and¦175812 he¦175812 died¦175812, just¦175813 as¦175813 the¦175815 man¦175815 of¦175815 God had said¦175818 when¦175819 the¦175820 king¦175820 \add ≈had gone to¦175821 his place\add*.
